cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Epagoge in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Epagoge"
abstract: >
  A graded synthetic corpus and curriculum for training a
  falsification-oriented foundation model. The corpus is generated and
  curated rather than scraped, and is written to a closed, self-hosting
  vocabulary in which every defined word reduces to a seed of words that
  are learned by being shown rather than defined. It is ordered as a
  difficulty-graded curriculum whose early levels present simplified
  concepts and whose later levels revisit them at increasing complexity.
  That such ordering improves pretraining is the hypothesis under test
  rather than a claim of the work.
authors:
  - family-names: "Sechter"
    given-names: "Brendan"
    email: "sgeos@hotmail.com"
url: "https://github.com/sgeos/epagoge"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sgeos/epagoge"
# Both, because the tree holds both. LICENSING.md says which applies
# where. The corpus is the artifact an academic would cite.
license:
  - "CC0-1.0"
  - "0BSD"
type: dataset
keywords:
  - "synthetic-data"
  - "pretraining"
  - "curriculum-learning"
  - "corpus"
  - "controlled-vocabulary"
  - "language-model"
  - "cc0"
